findings.body:
`rss.items.each` has no per-item error handling, so the first exception stops all remaining items on every run. Likely triggers include:
- a nil `content`;
- a deleted embed post;
- an `embed_url` longer than the 255-char varchar column;
- a unique-index race;
- `RateLimiter::LimitExceeded` when `embed_by_username` is not staff.

On the last point: topic creation is still rate-limited (e.g. `rate_limit_create_topic` of 5s) despite `skip_validations`, so a non-staff import user will typically fail on the second new item.

Because the same items come first on every hourly run, the feed can be permanently stuck. Rescue and log per item, and bypass or disable rate limiting for the import user, as the Disqus task does.
